E2E_TS11_TC002	DXP -> Account Dashboard (Desktop)	"1. Interested Party (Professional Contact / Trusted Advisor, Alpha) test user holding 2+ DAFs with different data.
2. DAF toggle unavailable condition for the [Error] steps (env condition)."	"Component: Dashboard Landing & Paths
(Happy Path + Negative Path)

Validate the multi-DAF / Trusted Advisor path: Account Selection to Dashboard, switching DAFs through the dashboard toggle, header switcher and Account Selection tab with data refreshing, and the DAF toggle unavailable state."	Step 1	Launch the DXP QA7/APINT portal URL.	Vanguard Charitable login page loads successfully.
				Step 2	Log in with valid multi-DAF Trusted Advisor credentials.	User lands on Account Selection (not the dashboard).
				Step 3	Select DAF A.	User lands on the Account Dashboard for DAF A; dropdown and header switcher show DAF A; ACCOUNT SELECTION tab visible.
				Step 4	Capture DAF A Current/Available Balance and latest Grant recipient.	Values stored in suite variables.
				Step 5	Refresh the browser.	Dashboard reloads on DAF A; dropdown and header switcher still show DAF A (selection persisted).
				Step 6	Open the dashboard account dropdown.	Overlay with X; all DAFs listed as '<Account No> - <Fund Name>', scrollable, no duplicates; 'Open Additional Account' link at the bottom.
				Step 7	Close with X, reopen and select DAF B.	Dropdown closes without change; selecting DAF B reloads the dashboard for DAF B with different balances/cards than DAF A.
				Step 8	Switch back to DAF A using the header account switcher.	Dashboard shows DAF A; values match those captured.
				Step 9	Click ACCOUNT SELECTION tab and select DAF B.	Account Selection page loads; selecting DAF B returns to the dashboard for DAF B.
				Step 10	[Error] With the DAF toggle unavailable, select another DAF from the dashboard dropdown.	Red banner 'Switching between accounts is not available from the dashboard at this time. Please use the account selector in the main navigation.'; dashboard stays on DAF B.
				Step 11	Switch via the header selector and dismiss the banner.	Switch succeeds; banner closes with no empty container.
